From 92a3c522b1165325a7dc88464856c6fa3a0b6be8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pierre Kisters <pierrekisters@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:54:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(java): import_file runs pre_scripts and post_scripts

A target that needs preparing before analysis (a raw COM image given its
segment) or fixing after it could not be imported through import_file:
the client had to import, then run a script on the saved program, and a
second client could see the half-prepared program in between.

pre_scripts run on the loaded program before its first save, post_scripts
after auto-analysis, each {path, args} like AnalyzeHeadless -preScript and
-postScript. A failing pre-script imports nothing; a failing post-script
removes the import, so a retry starts from the file. The response carries
script_output; /analysis_status reports a failed wait=false import.

Gated by GHIDRA_MCP_ALLOW_SCRIPTS like every other way to run a script,
and by the new GHIDRA_MCP_IMPORT_SCRIPT_ROOTS (a path list) when set.
Only absolute paths to .java files. Each script's directory is enabled as
its own bundle instead of being copied into ~/ghidra_scripts.

Script loads share one JVM-wide lock: Ghidra's bundle build takes a file
lock meant for separate JVMs, and two threads of one JVM failed with
OverlappingFileLockException. /run_ghidra_script took no lock and loaded
its script twice (getScriptInstance, then runScript(name)); it now
executes the instance it loaded, under the same lock.

Depends on the import loader options change (ImportRequest, finishImport)
and on the several-roots change (canonicalRoots/underAny).

Tests: ImportScriptsTest (request shape, the gate, roots, symlink),
ImportScriptsGhidraTest (real scripts: args, pre/post, failures leave
nothing behind, refusals, concurrent loads and concurrent
/run_ghidra_script, both failing without the lock), bridge payload and
poll tests. tests/endpoints.json edited by hand (no Maven here).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
