index 587f28d..e1f196f 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -8,6 +8,30 @@ Complete version history for the Ghidra MCP Server project.
 
 Changes on `dev` after 7.0.0.
 
+### Added — `import_file` runs pre- and post-scripts, as AnalyzeHeadless does
+
+A target that needs preparing before it is analyzed (a raw COM image given its segment, an
+analyzer option no loader argument covers, a no-return fix after analysis) could not be
+imported through `import_file`; the client had to import, then run a script on the saved
+program. `pre_scripts` run on the loaded program before its first save and analysis, and
+`post_scripts` after analysis, each `{"path": "/abs/Script.java", "args": [...]}` like
+`-preScript` / `-postScript`. A failing pre-script imports nothing; a failing post-script removes
+the import again, so a retry starts from the file. The response carries `script_output`; a
+`wait=false` import that fails is reported by `/analysis_status`.
+
+Scripts stay behind `GHIDRA_MCP_ALLOW_SCRIPTS`, and the new `GHIDRA_MCP_IMPORT_SCRIPT_ROOTS`
+(a path list) restricts them to vetted directories, so a server can run its own import scripts
+without clients naming arbitrary code. Only absolute paths to `.java` files are accepted. Each
+script's directory is enabled as its own bundle (not copied into `~/ghidra_scripts`).
+
+### Fixed — concurrent script runs collided in Ghidra's bundle build
+
+Ghidra guards a bundle build with a file lock meant for separate JVMs; two threads of one JVM
+building at once failed with `OverlappingFileLockException`. Every script load now takes one
+JVM-wide lock (`ImportScripts.LOAD_LOCK`). `/run_ghidra_script` also ran its script with
+`runScript(name, args)`, which loaded it a second time outside any lock; it now executes the
+instance it already loaded.
+
 ### Added — `import_file` takes the loader options AnalyzeHeadless takes
 
